## History

### 1.2 (16.11.2026)

- Icon view uses a scroller.gadget for its scroll bar, so it looks and
  works like the one in details mode (arrows, knob, GUI settings). The
  class opens `gadgets/scroller.gadget`; without it the old bar is drawn.
- Everything icon view draws is clipped to the gadget and to the inside
  of the window's borders: a scroll bar piece was once left on a
  window's status bar and border.

### 1.1 (15.11.2026)

- Dragging a selection box past the top or bottom of the view (which
  scrolls it) no longer draws lines of the box outside the view. The
  box's corner stays inside the view while it scrolls, so the box is
  always seen.
- The mouse wheel also scrolls while a selection box is dragged.
- Icon view paints the thin gaps around the cells and the scroll bar;
  bits of the list view showed through there after switching views.

### 1.0 (15.11.2026)

- First release.
